{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLineDefinition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLineDefinition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuarkState.WeakChiralityRootLabel"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.neg_flip_ne_braid_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.neg_flip_ne_braid_image","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L170-L178","doc":"**Well-posedness.** Given an index character with `χ σ = q > 0`, no braid word\n(a product of letters each sent to `q` or `q⁻¹`) equals `−σ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.index_prod_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.index_prod_pos","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L158-L168","doc":"Every product of letters valued `q` or `q⁻¹` by the index character is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.index_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.index_flip","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L152-L156","doc":"An index character sends `σ⁻¹` to `q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L137-L148","doc":"**5. Mirror**: with `σ⁻¹` as the positive crossing (parameter `q⁻¹`), the left line\nis the original right line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_eq_Pp_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_eq_Pp_iff","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L130-L135","doc":"**4. Regime dependence**: `leftLine = P₊` iff `|q| > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.weakVertex_mul_rightLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.weakVertex_mul_rightLine","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L122-L128","doc":"**2. On the right line the weak vertex acts as `σ`** (no flavour change). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.weakVertex_mul_leftLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.weakVertex_mul_leftLine","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L113-L120","doc":"**2. On the left line the weak vertex acts as `σ⁻¹`** (it changes flavour there). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_eigen_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_eigen_flip","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**3. Universality**, other flavour: `σ⁻¹` acts on the same line by a scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_eigen_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_eigen_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L99-L104","doc":"**3. Universality**, generator: `σ` acts on the left line by a scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.flip_eigenline_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.flip_eigenline_left","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L92-L97","doc":"**1. Flavour-blind**: the left line of `σ` is an eigenline of `σ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_neg_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_neg_inv","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L87-L90","doc":"**0. Label independence.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_add_rightLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_add_rightLine","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L81-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.rightLine_of_not_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.rightLine_of_not_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.rightLine_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.rightLine_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_of_not_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_of_not_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.weakVertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.weakVertex","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L69-L71","doc":"The one-sided flip on the left line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.rightLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.rightLine","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The complementary (right) line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.LeftLine.leftLine","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/LeftLineDefinition.lean#L60-L64","doc":"**Owner ruling 2026-11-15 (definition).** The left line is the eigenline on which the\npositive-crossing generator `σ` (a letter at parameter `q`) acts with eigenvalue of size\n`> 1`. At `|q| = 1` neither eigenvalue qualifies; the `else` branch is then only a\ndefault, and the label-independence lemma below excludes that case. ","signatureChunk":0}]}